ionPaths) && ... policy.regressionPaths.includes(finding.path)`;\n- `blocking = scheduledBlocking(finding, { round, regression })`;\n- `demoted: reviewerBlocking && !blocking`.\n\nHead boundary-review.js:42-47 builds blocks with `regression: sweptClassRegression(sweeps, finding, round) || (prior ? ... : regressionPaths.has(finding.path))`. Its records come from scopeSweepRecords (sweep-records.js:87-103), and the review input stores them as sweepRecords (execution.js:1178), so the projection could apply the same rule but does not.\n\nTarget PERFORMANCE.md:216 defines blocking as 'whether it blocked when raised under the round schedule'. The target's convergence-metrics.test.js:113-115 covers path regressions only, and no test covers swept-class demotion. The desktop mirror apps/desktop/resources/performance/workflow-projection.js carries the same code.\n\nThe path is in packet.roundPolicy.regressionPaths and the band is hand-back, so a medium here blocks.","failureScenario":"After merging into a9ce8b7, with metrics enabled (the default, store.js:7): round 4 or 5 qualifies a medium blocking finding whose classId matches a sweep record from a fixed claim, on a path not in regressionPaths. -> boundary-review.js:45-47 blocks it and the round FAILs, but workflow-projection.js:78-81 stores blocking:false, demoted:true. `metrics convergence` then counts as demoted a finding that actually blocked (demotedMeasure, escapedMeasure and the decided follow-up part), the reverse of PERFORMANCE.md:216's 'whether it blocked when raised under the round schedule'.","id":"CR11-1","path":"repository/plugin-src/shared/resources/performance/workflow-projection.js","severity":"medium"}],"gate":"review","historyAssessment":{"affected":[],"carryForwardReason":"Both IDs up for reconsideration (codex/R1-command-path-cases and codex/R1-valid-disputed-command-path) cover cli/test/sweep-records.test.js and the two command entry points. The head is still a66d1f2, the same tree round 10 reviewed. I